372/selection/59c9bd7a11b30424197b201962e88c86b9e705a972daafea05a670c6d3816426" "q-80372/selection/5f16d2c962949048f0e40aeb50916c8b5ff416b24a2729242dbdb81d3494e7b1" "q-80372/selection/64cc366013c781a738fa29e5e5d2bbe2980d2f7d7328dc8f0b7cfb10e56d8fca" "q-80372/selection/123af2f285de44dc3880f810bc0709183cc9fadc4d35176979c062e82ae88f30" "q-80372/selection/299bfc0d187a493afc8293c1d974b31d8aaaa01226e5ce95f8a8abbe58605c4d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-80372" :question/id #uuid "eca769bd-39e5-50f4-ad17-04a339efaee8" :question/math-academy-id "q-80372" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 8 \\\\ -4 & -6\\end{aligned}].$ You're given that ${\\lambda }_{1}=2$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=-2$ are the eigenvalues of $A$, and\n${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$, ${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ are the respective eigenvectors. Find the matrices $P$ and $D$ such that $PD{P}^{-1}=A,$ where $D$ is a diagonal matrix." :question/worked-solution "Since the eigenvalues of the matrix are ${\\lambda }_{1}=2$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=-2,$ we construct the diagonal matrix $D$ by writing the eigenvalues in the main diagonal:\n\n$$\nD=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, to construct the matrix $P,$ we simply write the respective eigenvectors as columns: \n\n- the $1$st column is the eigenvector corresponding to ${\\lambda }_{1}=2,$ and\n\n- the $2$nd column is the eigenvector corresponding to ${\\lambda }_{2}=-2.$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-80372/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5164c6cb-aef0-554b-b361-77245991c0ea"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-80372"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-80373/selection/9097ac8ebbd2f3c6a11507b6e553c335fb416735ff069dad799fe976ac7417cc" :answer/id #uuid "eabc05e8-0f13-