73" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $H$ for which ${\\lambda }_{1}=4$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=-2$ are eigenvalues, and\n\n$$\n{v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}],\\,{v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nare the respective eigenvectors. What are the values of $a,b,c$ given that\n\n$$\nH=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -3 \\\\ b & c\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & a\\end{aligned}]{[\\begin{aligned}5 & -3 \\\\ b & c\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Since the eigenvalues of the matrix are ${\\lambda }_{1}=4$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=-2,$ we construct the diagonal matrix $D$ by writing the eigenvalues in the main diagonal:\n\n$$\nD=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, to construct the matrix $P,$ we simply write the respective eigenvectors as columns: \n\n- the $1$st column is the eigenvector corresponding to ${\\lambda }_{1}=4,$ and\n\n- the $2$nd column is the eigenvector corresponding to ${\\lambda }_{2}=-2.$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -3 \\\\ 7 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\nH=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -3 \\\\ 7 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]{[\\begin{aligned}5 & -3 \\\\ 7 & 1\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn conclusion, we get  $a=-2,$ $b=7,$ and $c=1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-80373/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5164c6cb-aef0-554b-b361-77245991c0ea"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-80373"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-140039/selection/f8c96d1e9a8470c4d21627ed50926930ef5c4f59f3006901018a4c3e082a1383" :answer/id #uuid "17850b78-a0e8-5e3e-9890-d988acd7c78b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$a=2,$ $b=-2,$ and $c=3$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140039/selection/c9ff9df131f33e8e8a540d2d9424af9ffb7bdff7f7290c20dc7b72ec670b28ff" :answer/id #uuid "f6029480-361b-56ac