re the respective eigenvectors. What are the values of $a,b,c$ given that\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & b \\\\ c & -4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}a & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]{[\\begin{aligned}1 & b \\\\ c & -4\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Since the eigenvalues of the matrix are ${\\lambda }_{1}=-2$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=-1,$ we construct the diagonal matrix $D$ by writing the eigenvalues in the main diagonal:\n\n$$\nD=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, to construct the matrix $P,$ we simply write the respective eigenvectors as columns: \n\n- the $1$st column is the eigenvector corresponding to ${\\lambda }_{1}=-2,$ and\n\n- the $2$nd column is the eigenvector corresponding to ${\\lambda }_{2}=-1.$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -4\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn conclusion, we get $a=-2,$ $b=3,$ and $c=-2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-140039/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5164c6cb-aef0-554b-b361-77245991c0ea"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-140039"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-80455/selection/fde7c7e8c5c0e1280c4619c1897573fc8396a25055092e595f0052889d677717" :answer/id #uuid "853eec6a-d8ff-5b36-922a-3f60256d0bbb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$A$ is not diagonalizable" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80455/selection/d535b142166abc50b96bfd3158afbae683cde9f64ad2ff61578075f3e59402cd" :answer/id #uuid "b1e9745a-c762-5395-8a28-37815142b6a0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "D=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80455/selection/bf0de7bec337a18efe248bde3cfb378356757c51cc893771a68049d